# Origin of the Finora API, including the version prefix.
#
# Every VITE_* variable is inlined into the browser bundle at build time, so this file may
# only ever hold public values. API keys and secrets belong in the server's environment.
#
# Keep this RELATIVE (`/api/v1`) in every environment, including production. Requests then
# stay same-origin as the SPA, so the API's HttpOnly SameSite=Lax auth cookies are sent
# (a browser will NOT attach Lax cookies to a cross-site XHR). Something has to forward
# /api to the real API on each side:
#   - Development: the Vite dev proxy forwards /api → http://localhost:5000 (see vite.config.ts).
#   - Production (Vercel): the `rewrites` in vercel.json forward /api/* → the Render API host.
# See ARCHITECTURE.md §12. Only set an absolute origin here if you deliberately move the
# cookies to SameSite=None; Secure first — a documented §6 security-posture change, not a shortcut.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
